    <string name="faq_title">FAQ</string>
    <string name="faq_anti_flicker">HalfRotate locks system auto-rotate while running and rotates directly between allowed orientations — no flash through blocked angles.</string>
    <string name="faq_disabled_rotations">Enable only the rotations you want. 90° and 270° horizontal are separate. A disabled angle snaps to the nearest allowed one (90° ↔ 270°, 180° → 0°).</string>
    <string name="faq_app_orientation">Some apps force their own orientation and may ignore system rotation. HalfRotate applies to the Android system, which covers most apps.</string>
    <string name="faq_channels">Play Store and F-Droid builds use different signing keys. Switching stores requires reinstalling the app.</string>

